{% extends "_layouts/default.njk" %}

{% block content %}
  <div class="nhsuk-grid-row">
    <div class="nhsuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      <h1 class="nhsuk-heading-xl">Missing or incorrect details</h1>

      <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-l">Missing a dose</h2>

      <p>A child may be missing a dose, for example:</p>
      <ul class="nhsuk-list nhsuk-list--bullet">
        <li>if they were ill when they were due to have the dose, and have not yet had a catch-up dose</li>
        <li>if they were in another country when they were due to have the dose according to the UK schedule (and that country had a different vaccination schedule)</li>
      </ul>

      <p>If your child is missing a dose you can contact your GP or school age immunisation service (SAIS) for a catch-up dose.</p>

      <p>There are many reasons why a child may appear to be missing a dose which you think they’ve had, for example:</p>

      <ul class="nhsuk-list nhsuk-list--bullet">
        <li>they moved in from abroad and their vaccination details were lost, incomplete or hard to interpret</li>
        <li>they were vaccinated in hospital and the record wasn’t sent to the GP</li>
        <li>they had single measles, mumps and rubella vaccines, which do not count as MMR in most records</li>
        <li>they were vaccinated recently and the record has not yet reached us</li>
      </ul>

      <p>If you believe your child is up to date for their age but appears to be missing a dose in these records, contact your GP.</p>

      <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-l">Incorrect details</h2>

      <p>Some of the details may not be quite right, or may differ from the details in your child’s personal child health record (red book). For example, a child’s vaccination date may have been recorded as the date they were registered with the GP practice, or the date the vaccination was entered in the child’s record.</p>
      <p>If you think any of the information is incorrect, contact your GP.</p>

      <p>For other questions about your child’s vaccination record, read <a href="/parent-test/help-and-support">help and support</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
{% endblock %}
